<!-- this exercise was developed by Spencer Bagley as part of the PROTEUS grant-->

<p>
    In this section, we've considered the position of a ball and the ball's rate of change of position, which is called <em>velocity</em>. Respond to the following questions to explore the units, and therefore the meanings, of other rates of change.
</p>
<ol marker="a">
    <li>
        <p>
            The more people there are in a city, the more tax revenue is collected.
        </p>
        <p>
            <answer>
                <choiceInput shuffleOrder inline>
                    <label>The units for the independent variable might be </label>
                    <choice>dollars</choice>
                    <choice credit="1">people</choice>
                    <choice>meters</choice>
                    <choice>degrees Fahrenheit</choice>
                    <choice>meters per hour</choice>
                    <choice>hours</choice>
                </choiceInput>
            </answer>
        </p>
        <p>
            <answer>
                <choiceInput shuffleOrder inline>
                    <label>The units for the dependent variable might be </label>
                    <choice credit="1">dollars</choice>
                    <choice>people</choice>
                    <choice>meters</choice>
                    <choice>degrees Fahrenheit</choice>
                    <choice>meters per hour</choice>
                    <choice>hours</choice>
                </choiceInput>
            </answer>
        </p>
        <p>
            <answer matchPartial>
                <choiceInput shuffleOrder inline name="aRocNum">
                    <label>The units for the rate of change might be </label>
                    <choice>dollars</choice>
                    <choice>people</choice>
                    <choice>meters</choice>
                    <choice>degrees Fahrenheit</choice>
                    <choice>meters per hour</choice>
                    <choice>hours</choice>
                </choiceInput>
                <choiceInput shuffleOrder inline name="aRocDenom">
                    <label>per </label>
                    <choice>dollar</choice>
                    <choice>person</choice>
                    <choice>meter</choice>
                    <choice>degree Fahrenheit</choice>
                    <choice>meter per hour</choice>
                    <choice>hour</choice>
                </choiceInput>
                <award><when>
                    $aRocNum.selectedValues=<text>dollars</text> and
                    $aRocDenom.selectedValues=<text>person</text>
                </when></award>
            </answer>
        </p>
        <p>
            <answer type="text" handGraded expanded forceFullCheckWorkButton>
                <label>In your own words, what does the rate of change tell us about the city?</label>
            </answer>
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            As you ride in a rising hot air balloon, the temperature of the air around you decreases.
        </p>
        <p>
            <answer>
                <choiceInput shuffleOrder inline>
                    <label>The units for the independent variable might be </label>
                    <choice>dollars</choice>
                    <choice>people</choice>
                    <choice credit="1">meters</choice>
                    <choice>degrees Fahrenheit</choice>
                    <choice>meters per hour</choice>
                    <choice>hours</choice>
                </choiceInput>
            </answer>
        </p>
        <p>
            <answer>
                <choiceInput shuffleOrder inline>
                    <label>The units for the dependent variable might be </label>
                    <choice>dollars</choice>
                    <choice>people</choice>
                    <choice>meters</choice>
                    <choice credit="1">degrees Fahrenheit</choice>
                    <choice>meters per hour</choice>
                    <choice>hours</choice>
                </choiceInput>
            </answer>
        </p>
        <p>
            <answer matchPartial>
                <choiceInput shuffleOrder inline name="bRocNum">
                    <label>The units for the rate of change might be </label>
                    <choice>dollars</choice>
                    <choice>people</choice>
                    <choice>meters</choice>
                    <choice>degrees Fahrenheit</choice>
                    <choice>meters per hour</choice>
                    <choice>hours</choice>
                </choiceInput>
                <choiceInput shuffleOrder inline name="bRocDenom">
                    <label>per </label>
                    <choice>dollar</choice>
                    <choice>person</choice>
                    <choice>meter</choice>
                    <choice>degree Fahrenheit</choice>
                    <choice>meter per hour</choice>
                    <choice>hour</choice>
                </choiceInput>
                <award><when>
                    $bRocNum.selectedValues=<text>degrees Fahrenheit</text> and
                    $bRocDenom.selectedValues=<text>meter</text>
                </when></award>
            </answer>
        </p>
        <p>
            <answer type="text" handGraded expanded forceFullCheckWorkButton>
                <label>In your own words, what does the rate of change tell us about your hot air balloon ride?</label>
            </answer>
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            For a given trip of a particular distance, as the speed of the car increases, the travel time decreases.
        </p>
        <p>
            <answer>
                <choiceInput shuffleOrder inline>
                    <label>The units for the independent variable might be </label>
                    <choice>dollars</choice>
                    <choice>people</choice>
                    <choice>meters</choice>
                    <choice>degrees Fahrenheit</choice>
                    <choice credit="1">meters per hour</choice>
                    <choice>hours</choice>
                </choiceInput>
            </answer>
        </p>
        <p>
            <answer>
                <choiceInput shuffleOrder inline>
                    <label>The units for the dependent variable might be </label>
                    <choice>dollars</choice>
                    <choice>people</choice>
                    <choice>meters</choice>
                    <choice>degrees Fahrenheit</choice>
                    <choice>meters per hour</choice>
                    <choice credit="1">hours</choice>
                </choiceInput>
            </answer>
        </p>
        <p>
            <answer matchPartial>
                <choiceInput shuffleOrder inline name="cRocNum">
                    <label>The units for the rate of change might be </label>
                    <choice>dollars</choice>
                    <choice>people</choice>
                    <choice>meters</choice>
                    <choice>degrees Fahrenheit</choice>
                    <choice>meters per hour</choice>
                    <choice>hours</choice>
                </choiceInput>
                <choiceInput shuffleOrder inline name="cRocDenom">
                    <label>per </label>
                    <choice>dollar</choice>
                    <choice>person</choice>
                    <choice>meter</choice>
                    <choice>degree Fahrenheit</choice>
                    <choice>meter per hour</choice>
                    <choice>hour</choice>
                </choiceInput>
                <award><when>
                    $cRocNum.selectedValues=<text>hours</text> and
                    $cRocDenom.selectedValues=<text>meter per hour</text>
                </when></award>
            </answer>
        </p>
        <p>
            <answer type="text" handGraded expanded forceFullCheckWorkButton>
                <label>In your own words, what does the rate of change tell us about your trip?</label>
            </answer>
        </p>
    </li>
</ol>